# methanesulfonamide.msf
# Methanesulfonamide (CH3SO2NH2)
# pKa=10.100 (N-H sulfonamide acid, q=0→-1)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Simplest acyclic N-H sulfonamide. The SO2 group strongly withdraws
# electron density from N, making it much more acidic than a simple
# amine (pKa 10.1 vs ~10.6). Isolated from other ionisable groups.
# Reaction is standard H+ loss: CH3SO2NH2 → CH3SO2NH- + H+

